  ],
  "details": "<p>One of the Akkadian inscriptions is written in contemporary Neo-Babylonian script, while the other is engraved in archaizing Neo-Babylonian script.\u00a0</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Two rock reliefs with inscriptions of the Neo-Babylonian king Nebuchadnezzar II were engraved in the Wadi esh-Sharbin, about 2 km southwest of the modern Lebanese town Brissa (also called Bra\u00efss\u00e9, Brisa).",
